Today is Friday.
I am working in the office.
Vikram comes to my desk.
He is our software tester.
"Maya, I have checked your new code," Vikram says.
I ask, "Have you found any bugs?"
"Yes, I have found a few minor bugs," he says.
He shows me those bugs on my screen.
"But you have done very good work," Vikram says with a smile.
I appreciate his sharp eye.
He has done his work very well.
"Thank you Vikram, I will correct these bugs right now," I say.
I type quickly for a few minutes.
I have removed those bugs from the code.
"Vikram, I have corrected the code," I say.
Vikram looks at that code once again.
"Great, now this is absolutely correct," he says.
We both have completed this work on time.
